{"key":"1b96ea351de60d9f","source_file":"Potts Hi - Hy.json","source_id":62897,"source_url":"concordance-hypostatic-ppl-hypostaticus","term":"Hypostatic","headwords":["Hypostatic"],"latin":["Hypostaticus"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Hypostatic"],"latin":["Hypostaticus"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AR","CanonsNC","ConvCalvin","TCR"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AR","section":"565","subsection":"2"},"text":"Which is called the hypostatic union, are meant...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"94","subsection":"2"},"text":"They who by the hypostatic union understand a union as between two, of whom one is above and the other below. TCR 137:10.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"174","subsection":"2"},"text":"It was devised... that there was Divinity in His Human by the hypostatic union...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"ConvCalvin","section":"2","subsection":"7"},"text":"I asked about the hypostatic union... Calvin said that it was from God the Father...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"CanonsNC","section":"16","subsection":null},"text":"Redeemer. 2. Note. The hypostatic Word.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"CanonsNC","section":"16","subsection":null},"text":"Redeemer. 2. 6. The hypostatic Word is nothing but the Divine truth.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"hypostatic","url":"/meta/potts/hypostatic/"}